---
import Layout from '~/layouts/Layout.astro'
---

<Layout title="Product Template">
  <div class="mt-header h-48 lg:h-96">
    <img
      class="h-full w-full select-none object-cover"
      src="/images/jake-forsher-4-HydgF5dM8-unsplash.jpg"
      alt="A man holding a gun"
    />
  </div>

  <div class="py-16 lg:py-24">
    <div class="mx-auto max-w-screen-xl px-4 md:px-8">
      <div class="flex max-w-screen-md flex-col gap-4 lg:gap-6">
        <div class="flex flex-col gap-3">
          <p class="text-sm font-semibold text-brand-700 lg:text-md dark:text-dark-300">
            Training Course
          </p>
          <h1
            class="font-display text-display-md font-semibold lg:text-display-lg dark:text-light-50"
          >
            Shotgun Defense LVL1 Class
          </h1>
        </div>

        <p class="text-lg text-light-600 lg:text-xl dark:text-dark-400">
          The Pump Action Shotgun is one of the most misunderstood firearms. The pump action shotgun
          offers flexibility in selection of ammunition for different objectives. In this course
          will learn the safe deployment of a pump action shotgun and develop the Combat Mindset for
          crisis survival. This course will include basic shotgun fundamentals, patterning and
          ammunition selection, malfunction clearances, carry methods and cleaning and maintenance.
          The shotgun as a home defense firearm will be covered and the student will learn basic
          home defense tactics.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="pb-16 lg:pb-24">
    <div class="mx-auto max-w-screen-xl px-4 md:px-8">
      <div class="grid gap-8 xl:grid-cols-12">
        <div class="prose dark:prose-invert xl:col-span-8">
          <h2>What you will learn:</h2>
          <ul>
            <li>Nomenclature</li>
            <li>Cycle of Operation</li>
            <li>Loading and UnloadingDisassembly/Assembly/Maintenance</li>
            <li>Shotgun Carries</li>
            <li>Malfunctions and Stoppages</li>
            <li>Marksman Fundamentals</li>
            <li>Firing Positions and Stance</li>
            <li>Ammunition and Patterning</li>
          </ul>

          <h2>You will need the following equipment for the class:</h2>
          <ol>
            <li>Pump action Shotgun (12ga. Or 20 ga.) with attached sling</li>
            <li>No Pistol Grip only shotguns</li>
            <li>Ammunition</li>
            <li>25 rounds of 00 buckshot or #4 buck</li>
            <li>25 Rifled Slug</li>
            <li>100 rounds of birdshot (#6, #7 or #8 shot)</li>
            <li>Ammunition pouch (a way to carry extra ammo on person)</li>
            <li>Eye and Ear protection</li>
            <li>Shotgun cleaning kit</li>
            <li>Sturdy belt</li>
            <li>Comfortable range attire (dress for the elements)</li>
            <li>Comfortable shoes (no sandals or Crocs)</li>
            <li>Ball cap or Boonie style hat</li>
            <li>Note taking material</li>
            <li>Knee and elbow pads (optional)</li>
            <li>Snacks, water, lunch</li>
            <li>Sunblock</li>
          </ol>

          <h2>Instructor's Bio</h2>
          <p>
            Ron Clayton is currently employed with a local Sheriff's Department with 25 years of
            experience as a law enforcement officer, with a varied list of assignments including
            SWAT, FTO, Patrol, Detectives and Academy Instructor. He is a FBI certified firearm
            instructor, California POST Rifle instructor, Defensive Tactics instructor and Stop the
            Bleed instructor.
          </p>
          <p>
            Ron recently retired from the California Air National Guard after 22 years of service
            (Active and Reserve) including 4 deployments in support of Operation Iraqi Freedom and
            Operation Enduring Freedom. During his deployments, he was assigned as a Dedicated
            Marksman and Combat LifeSaver. While at home station, Ron taught M4 rifle, M9 handgun,
            and M870 shotgun, Urban Environment Tactics, Concealed Carry, Trauma Care and Combative.
            As a member of the California Emergency Response and Force Protection Training Cadre,
            Ron assisted in developing the training curriculum for National Guard members responding
            to civil disturbances and natural disasters. He also was the lead instructor to Ukraine
            in the National Guard's Partnership for Peace program, sharing western style Law
            Enforcement and Tactics to the Ukraine military.
          </p>
          <p>
            His hobbies include reading about history, shooting, martial arts and currently holds a
            black belt (2nd Dan) in Taiho Jutsu and has trained in Krav Maga and Brazilian Ju Jitsu.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div class="prose dark:prose-invert xl:col-span-4">
          <div class="not-prose flex flex-col">
            <h2 class="font-display text-display-sm font-semibold text-light-900 dark:text-dark-50">
              $249.00
            </h2>
            <div class="text-xl text-light-700 dark:text-dark-300">From 8:30 AM to 3:30 PM</div>
          </div>

          <div>
            <!-- form -->
          </div>

          <p>
            All persons using the Piru Holding LLC Public Shooting Range must carefully read,
            understand the <span class="text-brand-600 dark:text-brand-500">
              Tactical Training Rules & Disclaimer
            </span> and agree in order to participate.
          </p>
          <p>
            CTA reserves the right to cancel any course. Any notification sent to fully paid
            customers will be done so within a 48 hour advance notice. Due to Law Enforcement
            contracts with the State of California, CTA reserves the right to withhold cause or
            reason for cancellations. CTA reserves the right to refuse participants for any reason.
            CTA is not responsible for any non-refundable expenses incurred by you or any other
            persons as a result of your registration, attendance, non-attendance, or
            self-cancellation of any course.
          </p>

          <h3 class="not-prose mb-2 font-semibold text-light-900 dark:text-dark-50">
            Cancellation Policy
          </h3>
          <p>
            In order to receive full refund we require a notice of at least 5 days before the course
            date.
          </p>

          <div class="not-prose inline-flex items-center gap-2">
            <input
              class="form-checkbox cursor-pointer rounded bg-transparent text-brand-600 transition-all focus:ring-4 focus:ring-brand-600/25 focus:ring-offset-0"
              type="checkbox"
              id="agree"
            />
            <label
              class="cursor-pointer text-sm font-semibold text-light-700 dark:text-dark-300"
              for="agree"
            >
              I agree to the Terms & Conditions
            </label>
          </div>

          <div class="not-prose mt-5 flex flex-col">
            <a
              class="rounded bg-brand-600 px-4 py-2.5 text-center font-semibold text-white transition-colors hover:bg-brand-700 focus:border-brand-400 focus:outline-none focus:ring-4 focus:ring-brand-600/25"
              href="#"
            >
              Book now
            </a>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</Layout>
